<title>Graph-Based Code Agent</title>


<div class=3D"wrap">

  <header class=3D"masthead">
    <div class=3D"eyebrow">RapidLR Code Agent =C2=B7 Architecture Proposal<=
/div>
    <h1>A Graph-Based Redesign for the Code Agent</h1>
    <p class=3D"subhead">The current Code Agent fetches one file by filenam=
e and asks an LLM four fixed questions about it. That works when the bug li=
ves in the file the ticket happens to name. Most real bugs don't stay put =
=E2=80=94 they live in the path between files. Here's a version that follow=
s that path.</p>
  </header>

  <section class=3D"block">
    <h2><span class=3D"num">01</span> Where the single-file design breaks</=
h2>
    <div class=3D"frailty-grid">
      <div class=3D"frailty-card">
        <h3>One file, no path</h3>
        <p>The lookup is <code>business_unit =3D=3D X AND filename startswi=
th Y</code> =E2=80=94 it returns exactly one file. If the actual defect is =
in a shared validator or a config-resolution function that file calls, the =
agent never sees it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"frailty-card">
        <h3>Brittle key matching</h3>
        <p>Retrieval depends on the ticket naming a clean business_unit + c=
ountry pair. Real tickets are messier =E2=80=94 "why is response business n=
ot being stamped for some shortcodes" names no file at all.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"frailty-card">
        <h3>Filename-level embeddings</h3>
        <p>The Vector Search index embeds on <code>filename</code>, not on =
function content =E2=80=94 so even the semantic fallback can't find the rig=
ht function, only the right-sounding file.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"frailty-card">
        <h3>No verification</h3>
        <p>The LLM's answer is trusted as-is. Nothing re-checks the claimed=
 root cause against an actual failing record from <code>query_log_view</cod=
e> =E2=80=94 so a plausible-sounding wrong answer looks identical to a corr=
ect one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class=3D"block">
    <h2><span class=3D"num">02</span> The shape of the fix</h2>
    <p>Two changes, and they reinforce each other: replace the flat file st=
ore with a <strong>code graph</strong> (functions and config keys as nodes,=
 calls/reads as edges), and replace the one-shot chain with an <strong>agen=
t that can walk it</strong> =E2=80=94 hop from the entry point to whatever =
it actually calls, instead of stopping at the first file.</p>

    <figure class=3D"diagram">
      <svg viewBox=3D"0 0 920 380" role=3D"img" aria-label=3D"Comparison: t=
he current design does one filtered lookup into a single file and hands it =
to the LLM once; the proposed design resolves an entry point, walks the cal=
l graph outward, assembles multi-file context, lets an agent request more h=
ops, and verifies the answer against a real log record before returning it.=
">
