    <div class=3D"plan-wrap">
      <table class=3D"plan">
        <tbody><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Today</th><th>Proposed</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Code store</td><td><code>git_index_raw</code> Delta table, =
one row per file</td><td>Code graph: function/method nodes + config-key nod=
es, <code>calls</code> / <code>reads_config</code> edges, still Delta-backe=
d (edge + node tables) so it stays queryable from Spark</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Exact filter on <code>business_unit</code=
> + filename prefix</td><td>Function-level embeddings (GraphRAG-style) reso=
lve an entry point even from a vague ticket, then graph traversal takes ove=
r from there</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reasoning</td><td>One static prompt, four fixed questions, =
one file</td><td>LangGraph ReAct loop with tools (<code>get_function</code>=
, <code>get_callers</code>, <code>get_config_value</code>, <code>trace_data=
_flow</code>) =E2=80=94 agent decides how many hops it needs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trust</td><td>LLM's claim returned as-is</td><td>Verificati=
on step: pull the actual failing record via <code>query_log_view</code> and=
 re-check the claimed condition against it before returning RCA</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Index freshness</td><td>CI-triggered re-index on commit (ke=
pt as-is)</td><td>Same trigger, but the parse step now also rebuilds the ca=
ll/config-edge graph, not just the file row</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
